    "intro_html":  "Kuku paka comes off the Swahili coast, where Indian spice trading and East African cooking met and stayed together. Chicken gets browned first, then finishes in a coconut and tomato sauce built on cumin, coriander and turmeric. It is milder than an Indian curry and brighter than a Thai one, and it is one of those dishes that improves overnight without any help from you. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
